      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that’s exactly what this change is doing.\n\nBy adding `--lockfile_mode\u003derror` to our default Bazel flags, the build now enforces strict synchronization between `MODULE.bazel` and `MODULE.bazel.lock`.\n\nIf `MODULE.bazel` changes in a way that would require updating the lockfile, Bazel fails the build and prints actionable feedback, e.g.:\n\n```\n... not permitted with --lockfile_mode\u003derror.\nPlease run `bazel mod deps --lockfile_mode\u003dupdate` to update your lockfile.\n```\n\nSo we already get the “generated lock file is different -\u003e provide feedback” behavior, and we avoid silently rewriting `MODULE.bazel.lock` during normal builds. Updating the lockfile remains an explicit, intentional step via:\n\n```\n $\u003e bazelisk mod deps --lockfile_mode\u003dupdate\n```",
